  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/palaemon_concinnus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The bright white \"shear-fingers\" are very remarkable and give this species, imported from Sri Lanka, a special attraction.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/palaemon_concinnus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Palaemon concinnus can be found over an enormous range that includes nearly the entire Indo-Pacific. Origin: coastal regions of the Indo-Pacific. The species was first designated as Macrobrachium \"White Fingers\".</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/palaemon_concinnus_en/",
      "html": "<p>It is a rather delicate, smaller species, so one could try to keep it together with small fish. Because it is a newly imported species, no information is available on its behaviour in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/palaemon_concinnus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Because it is a newly imported species, no information is available on its breeding.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/palaemon_concinnus_en/",
      "html": "<p>An opportunity to break new ground is offered here to the crustacean enthusiast, and surely interesting discoveries will follow.</p>"
    }
